+C***********************************************************************
+C
+C     SolveConicIntersection - Shared conic ray-surface intersection solver
+C
+C     Purpose:
+C       Solves ray-conic surface intersection with robust numerical methods.
+C       This is the common implementation used by ConSrf, MonSrf, AsphSrf, etc.
+C
+C     Algorithm:
+C       1. Compute quadratic coefficients a*L^2 + b*L + c = 0
+C       2. Handle linear case (a ≈ 0)
+C       3. Check discriminant for real roots
+C       4. Detect near-tangent rays (discriminant ≈ 0)
+C       5. Use catastrophic cancellation avoidance
+C       6. Select appropriate root based on ifLNsrf flag
+C       7. Compute intersection point and surface normal
+C       8. Validate normal with NaN detection
+C       9. Check IEEE exceptions
+C
+C     Numerical Stability Features:
+C       - Catastrophic cancellation avoidance (TOL_CANCEL)
+C       - Near-tangent detection (TOL_TANGENT)
+C       - Overflow-safe root selection metric
+C       - IEEE NaN detection
+C       - IEEE exception handling
+C
+C     Author: Extracted from ConSrf/MonSrf harmonization
+C     Date: January 24, 2026
+C
 C***********************************************************************
 
-! Input arguments: pin, ihat, ifLNsrf
-! Output argments: pr, Nvec, Nmag, Nhat
